message: "Please cite this research package and the primary 2026 sources credited in the manuscript."
title: "Hyperplane Slices of the Marked-Cubic Map: A Classification and Geometric Explanation of the Three-Dimensional Keller Counterexample"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-27
authors:
  - family-names: Pitchford
    given-names: Ian
    contribution: "Research direction and geometric problem formulation"
  - name: "GPT-5.6 Pro (OpenAI)"
    contribution: "Proof synthesis, manuscript, and exact verifier"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipitchford/hermes-workspace/tree/research/jacobian-hyperplane-slices/research/jacobian-hyperplane-slices"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Jacobian conjecture
  - Keller map
  - binary cubic
  - resultant
  - etale morphism
  - twisted cubic
  - affine line bundle
abstract: >-
  A complete classification of normalized linear-times-quadratic factorization
  slices associated with affine hyperplanes in the space of binary cubics.
  The source is affine three-space exactly for tangent nonosculating
  hyperplanes. The package includes a coordinate-free geometric proof and an
  exact symbolic verifier for the announced polynomial counterexample.
